When the user asks to refactor custom code, improve architecture, apply SOLID, improve dependency injection, create interfaces, improve tests, or remove bad practices, use an OpenSpec change before implementation.

Read `.cursor/rules/00-openspec-stack-agnostic.mdc` and the target project's stack rule for source path layout.

Scope by default: application-owned source documented in the project (not vendor/contrib).

Out of scope by default: third-party dependencies, unrequested behavior changes, unjustified schema changes, cosmetic-only refactors.

Required analysis: missing interfaces, concrete coupling, weak mocks, service locators, god classes, logic in entry points, duplicated rules, insufficient tests.

Refactor rules: preserve behavior; minimal diffs; constructor injection; interface-based dependencies in tests and consumers.

Before implementation: OpenSpec proposal, tests, acceptance criteria, rollback, READY TO APPLY gate.

Never apply a SOLID refactor unless the spec is READY TO APPLY.
